---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { StudioScreen } from '../components/Studio/StudioScreen'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Studio — MorseForge"
  description="Render a message as Morse and record it."
  path="/studio/"
  private
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-14">
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Studio</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Type a message, pick a look and a size, and record it. Everything happens in this tab — the
      audio is the same engine the site teaches with, so what you hear is real CW at the speed
      shown.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10">
      <StudioScreen client:load />
    </div>

    <section class="mt-14 border-t border-line pt-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
      <p>
        The file is MP4 where the browser can record one, which is most of them now. That is not
        about compatibility but about correctness: MediaRecorder&rsquo;s WebM output carries no
        duration in its header, so anything that wants a frame rate divides frames by a duration of
        roughly zero and concludes the video runs at hundreds of frames per second. X rejects that
        outright &mdash; <em>maximum frame rate 60, actual 991</em> &mdash; even though the file was 60fps
        all along. An MP4 is finalised with a real duration, so it uploads without argument.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4">
        If your browser falls back to WebM and something refuses it, rewriting the container fixes
        it without re-encoding:
      </p>
      <pre
        class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-line bg-elevated p-4 font-mono text-xs">ffmpeg -i morseforge.webm -c copy -fflags +genpts morseforge.mp4</pre>
      <p class="mt-4">
        And if a platform still argues, this re-encodes at an explicit 60fps, which nothing refuses:
      </p>
      <pre
        class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-line bg-elevated p-4 font-mono text-xs">ffmpeg -i morseforge.webm -vf fps=60 -c:v libx264 -pix_fmt yuv420p -c:a aac morseforge.mp4</pre>
      <p class="mt-4">
        This page is not linked from anywhere, is disallowed in robots.txt and carries a noindex.
        The password on it is the part that actually protects it.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
